    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="Epilog">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIAs">II As</ref> Epilog</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="II As. Epilog" corresp="#wit-ld"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_Epilog.lnote.oe.1"/><pb n="166" ed="#liebermann"/>Ealle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_Epilog.lnote.oe.2"/> ðis wæs gesetted on ðam miclan synoþ<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_Epilog.lnote.oe.2"/> æt Greatanleage; on þam wæs se ærcebisceop Wulfhelme<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_Epilog.lnote.oe.2"/> mid eallum þæm æþelum mannum ⁊ wiotan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_Epilog.lnote.oe.2"/>, ðe Æþelstan cyning<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IIAs_Epilog.lnote.oe.star"/> gegadrian.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_Epilog.lnote.oe.3"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="II As. Epilog" corresp="#wit-q"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_Epilog.lnote.oe.1-2"/><pb n="167" ed="#liebermann"/>Totum hoc institutum (et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_Epilog.lnote.oe.2-2"/> confirmatum) est in magna<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_Epilog.lnote.oe.3-2"/> synodo apud Greateleyam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_Epilog.lnote.oe.4"/>, cui archiepiscopus Wulfhelmus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IIAs_Epilog.lnote.oe.5"/> interfuit et omnes optimates<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IIAs_Epilog.lnote.oe.6"/> et sapientes quos Æþelstanus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IIAs_Epilog.lnote.oe.7"/> rex congregare potuit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="142" ed="#attenborough"/>[Ealle ðis wæs gesetted on ðam miclan synoþ æt Greatanleage; on þam wæs se ærcebisceop Wulfhelme mid eallum þæm æþelum mannum ⁊ wiotan, ðe Æþelstan cyning mihte<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#IIAs_Epilog.attnote.fn.7"/> gegadrian.]<ptr type="editorNote" n="8" target="#IIAs_Epilog.attnote.fn.8"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="167" ed="#liebermann"/>(<hi rend="italic">Epilog</hi>. All dies wurde festgesetzt auf der grossen Reichsversammlung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_Epilog.lnote.de.1"/> zu Greatley<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_Epilog.lnote.de.2"/>; in ihr war der Erzbischof Wulfhelm<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_Epilog.lnote.de.2"/> mit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_Epilog.lnote.de.2"/> all den adligen Männern und Witan, welche König Aethelstan versammeln konnte. <hi rend="italic">Ld Quadr</hi>.)</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Epilogue. All this was established at the great assembly at Greatley; at it was Archbishop Wulfhelm with all the noble men and witan whom King Æthelstan could gather. Ld Quadr.)</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="143" ed="#attenborough"/>All this was established at the great assembly at Grately<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_Epilog.attnote.n.1"/>, at which Archbishop Wulfhelm<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_Epilog.attnote.n.2"/> was present, with all the nobles and councillors whom King Æthelstan had assembled.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="423" ed="#whitelock"/>[All this was established at the great assembly at Grately, at which Archbishop Wulfhelm was present and all the nobles and councillors whom King Athelstan could gather together.]<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_Epilog.whinote.n.1"/></ab>
        <note type="editorial">Only in Ld and Quadr. Ld lacks ‘mihte’, which Liebermann supplies from Quadr. (cf. V As 4?). Schmid numbers the epilogue 26.3.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_Epilog.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">166</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_Epilog.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">166</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze</hi> þe <hi rend="italic">aus Quadr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply þe from Quadr.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_Epilog.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">166</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze</hi> mihte [<hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> 4] <hi rend="italic">aus Quadr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply mihte [cf. 4] from Quadr.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_Epilog.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">166</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgt</hi> V As.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">followed by V As.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_Epilog.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">167</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">hinter</hi> IV As. <hi rend="italic">und vor</hi> III As. <hi rend="italic">Text aus K; Orthographie aus M; fehlt R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">after IV As. and before III As. Text from K; spelling from M; lacking in R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_Epilog.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">167</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lond;</hi> Epistola Æ. ad omnes sibi subiectos <hi rend="italic">roth T; keine Überschr. MHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Lond; Epistola Æ. ad omnes sibi subiectos in red T; no heading MHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_Epilog.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">167</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Aelst. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Aelst. Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_Epilog.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">167</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vor der Klammer Lesart Lond; eingeklammert Lesart der übrigen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">before the bracket the reading of Lond; in brackets the reading of the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_Epilog.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">167</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">modo <hi rend="italic">Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">modo Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_Epilog.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">167</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Grat. <hi rend="italic">KOr;</hi> Grect. <hi rend="italic">M;</hi> Greatt. <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Grat. KOr; Grect. M; Greatt. T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_Epilog.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">167</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eum <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eum K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_Epilog.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">107</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. Gl</hi> Witan 1 a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">See <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Witan 1 a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_Epilog.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">107</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. o.</hi> Einl. 5 und 3 über die Anthentizität des Epilogs</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">See above Introduction 5 and 3 on the authenticity of the epilogue</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIAs_Epilog.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">209</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">South-west of Andover, Hampshire.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIAs_Epilog.attnote.n.2" n="2" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">209</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">See I As. Pr., note 1.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_Epilog.attnote.fn.7" n="7" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">142</biblScope></bibl><label>mihte</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">om. Ld; supplied from Quadr. (<hi rend="italic">congregare potuit</hi>).</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_Epilog.attnote.fn.8" n="8" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">142</biblScope></bibl><label>gegadrian</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="IIAs_Epilog.whinote.n.1" n="1" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">423</biblScope></bibl><label>together.]</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">This is only in the Latin of <hi rend="italic">Quadripartitus,</hi> but may come from a lost prologue to the code. Lambard translated the Latin into Old English. Athelstan’s other legislation refers several times to the laws promulgated at Grately.</seg></note>
      </div>
